EEG dataset converted automatically to BIDS format using MATLAB.
This dataset was created from EEG recordings obtained from 40 stroke patients.
The identifying information of all patients has been anonymized..
Patients coded as (01AA, 06AA, 09CU, 11DD, 12DC, 13ES, 17FY, 18HT, 22KG, 24LA, 27NK, 32SA, 34UA) are classified as LEFT-SIDED PARALYSIS, while the others consist of RIGHT-SIDED PARALYSIS patients.
Each patient was asked to perform 16 different movements. These movements include:(RightLeg Up, RightLeg Down, RightLeg Open, RightLeg Close, LeftLeg Up, LeftLeg Down, LeftLeg Open, LeftLeg Close, RightArm Up).
The patients’ responses to these movement commands were categorized as either “Thinking” (performing the “Deep” movement by merely thinking about it) or “Movement” (attempting to perform the “Motor” movement).
The letters D and M at the beginning of the files indicate the “Deep” and “Motor” processes, respectively.
Patients were asked to repeat these tasks a maximum of 6 times, and they were given 10 seconds to complete each task.
The DEEP and MOTOR EEG recordings for all of the patients’ trials have been compiled into separate edf files, and the start times of each movement within the edf files are shown in the “task-motor_events.json” and “task-motor_events.tsv” files.
10-second interval starting from the onset time of the movements listed here was recorded as the EEG recording for that movement.
All patients’ EEG recordings were obtained from 25 EEG channels configured according to the EEG-10-20 standard. 
The EEG channel names correspond to the first 25 channels listed in the “motor_channels.tsv” files.
The EEG coordinate system is provided in the motor_coordsystem.json file.
Information regarding patient details can be obtained from the authors or by contacting the authors.
When using this dataset, please cite the following publication.
STREEG TEAM.
Dataset prepared for OpenNeuro submission.
